    "body": "## Summary\n\n- Second attempt at the invisible `M-x` text in `sp-mini-frame`. The minibuffer now remaps its `default` face to the foreground and background of the theme of the frame it was opened from (`sp-mini-frame--fix-colors` on `minibuffer-setup-hook`), so the text no longer depends on the child frame's own parameters.\n- New doc section \"Text colours of the minibuffer\" in `sp-mini-frame.org`, tangled into `sp-mini-frame.el`.\n- CHANGELOG entry added.\n\n## Not tested\n\n- Not run in Emacs (no GUI/macOS here); only tangled and paren-balanced.\n- Whether the text becomes visible on macOS is unconfirmed.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01MfEFZ7KDkwwcifErLfjf4X)_",
